{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Before a single [Dm7]star was hung, before the [Ebmaj7]hills were made
[Bb]God spoke a word into [Dm7]the dark and all the worlds [Ebmaj7]obeyed
[Bb]The things we see were fashioned [Dm7]out of what no eye had [Ebmaj7]seen
[Dm7]By faith we un[Gm7]derstand it, and on that [Cm7]word we lean
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F7sus4]Faith is the [Bb]assurance of what we hope [Dm7]for
The conviction of what [Ebmaj7]we do not see
Faith is [Bb]the assurance of what we hope [Dm7]for
The conviction of what [Ebmaj7]we do not see
It was by [Cm7]faith that [F7sus4]the people of old received God's ap[Bb]proval
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Abel brought a better [Dm7]gift and God called him right[Ebmaj7]eous
[Bb]Though he is dead, his faith still [Dm7]speaks across the years to [Ebmaj7]us
[Bb]Enoch walked to please the [Dm7]Lord and never did see [Ebmaj7]death
[Dm7]God took him up and he was not [Gm]found, gone like a morning [Cm7]breath
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Faith is [Bb]the assurance of what we hope [Dm7]for
The conviction of what [Ebmaj7]we do not see
Faith is [Bb]the assurance of what we hope [Dm7]for
The conviction of what [Ebmaj7]we do not see
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Dm7]Without faith it is impos[Gm]sible to please him
[Cm7]Whoever comes to God must be[F7sus4]lieve that he exists
[Cm7]And that he rewards [F7sus4]those who seek [Bb]him
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Faith is the assurance of what we hope [Dm7]for
